    "operation": {
      "body": "On ordinary open sand, sifting takes 2,400 work for one spice and produces half the deposit-harvesting vibration. This offers a slow fallback when no blow is available; it still occupies workers and exposes the machine."
    },
    "overview": {
      "body": "Spice prospecting research unlocks the extractor. Place it on a live deposit to gather two spice per 90 mining work, then haul the cargo before the deposit is exhausted or the work site becomes unsafe."
    },
    "risk": {
      "body": "The extractor’s disturbance can draw a Maker. A distant stockpile, blocked route or wounded worker can turn an otherwise short withdrawal into a dangerous delay. Abandoning equipment may be safer than waiting for one more load."
    },
